   "Statement": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\">\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\r\n\t<head>\r\n\t\t<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" /><title>\r\n\t\t</title>\r\n\t\t<style type=\"text/css\">\r\n\t\t\t.cs778DBFE2{text-align:left;text-indent:0pt;margin:5pt 0pt 5pt 0pt;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto}\r\n\t\t\t.csAC9CF2{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:21pt;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t\t.cs5E98E930{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t\t.csA16174BA{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;}\r\n\t\t\t.csD007A21A{color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;}\r\n\t\t</style>\r\n\t</head>\r\n\t<body>\r\n\t\t<p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Education: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">JD, Seattle University School of Law; BA with honors, Anthropology, California State University Long Beach</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Occupation: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">King County District Court Judge Pro Tem; Practicing Attorney</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><strong><span class=\"cs5E98E930\">Statement: </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Heather M. Barker has served as a Judge Pro Tem in King County District Court since 2022. &nbsp;She presides over both civil and criminal matters, including Mental Health and Veterans Courts. &nbsp;Through her judicial service, Heather has earned the trust of defense and prosecuting attorneys alike&mdash;and the endorsement of every judge in King County District Court&rsquo;s Southeast Division. </span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">An attorney for twelve years, Heather has owned a civil litigation firm for over a decade. &nbsp;She brings courtroom experience and business leadership. Born and raised in Kent, and now raising her family in Renton, the Southeast Division is Heather&rsquo;s hometown. &nbsp;She is a mom and proud spouse of an Army Veteran. &nbsp;Since graduation, she has drafted free estate plans for Washington first responders. She also volunteers with the YMCA Mock Trial program. </span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Heather believes that fair, thoughtful justice builds stronger, safer communities. She is committed to protecting public safety from the bench by carefully balancing accountability with rehabilitation. &nbsp;She is rated </span></strong></em><em><span class=\"csD007A21A\" style= \"font-style: italic;\">&ldquo;Exceptionally Well Qualified&rdquo; </span></strong></em><span class=\"csA16174BA\">by the King County Bar Association.</span></strong></em></p><p class=\"cs778DBFE2\"><span class=\"csA16174BA\">Endorsed: </span></strong></em><em><span class=\"csD007A21A\" style= \"font-style: italic;\">King County Police Officers Guild; National Women&rsquo;s Political Caucus; IAM&amp;AW 751; ATU 587; King County &amp; 5th, 11th, 30th, 31st, 33rd, 37th, and 47th LD Democrats; 35+ local judges. &nbsp;</span></strong></em></p></body>\r\n</html>\r\n",
